  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The modulus function, composite functions, inverses, and domain and range.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Functions",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\( |x|=c \\) gives \\( x=\\pm c \\). A composite \\( fg(x)=f(g(x)) \\) is applied inside-out. The inverse \\( f^{-1} \\) reverses \\( f \\); swap \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) and solve. The range of \\( f \\) is the domain of \\( f^{-1} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Modulus",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( |x|=\\pm c \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Composite",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( fg(x)=f(g(x)) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Inverse",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "swap \\( x,y \\) &amp; solve",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Range",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "output values",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the inverse of \\( f(x)=2x+1 \\).</p><p>Let \\( y=2x+1 \\), swap and solve:</p>\\[ f^{-1}(x)=\\tfrac{x-1}{2}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\( |x-1|=3 \\).</p>\\[ x=4,\\ -2. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Given \\(f(x)=2x-3\\) for \\(x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\), sketch \\(y=|f(x)|\\) and solve \\(|2x-3|=5\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Sketch: V-shape with vertex at \\((1.5,0)\\). Solve: \\(2x-3=5\\Rightarrow x=4\\) or \\(2x-3=-5\\Rightarrow x=-1\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "figure",
        "figure": {
          "type": "fn",
          "fns": [
            { "fn": "abs(2*x - 3)", "label": "y = |2x - 3|" }
          ],
          "points": [
            { "x": 1.5, "y": 0, "label": "Vertex (1.5, 0)" },
            { "x": 0, "y": 3, "label": "y-intercept (0, 3)" },
            { "x": 4, "y": 5, "label": "(4, 5)" },
            { "x": -1, "y": 5, "label": "(-1, 5)" }
          ],
          "xrange": [-3, 5],
          "yrange": [-1, 7]
        },
        "caption": {
          "en": "Graph of the modulus function y = |2x - 3|, showing the vertex on the x-axis and intersection points with y = 5.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "⚠️ Cambridge 9709 Traps — Modulus Inequalities & Extraneous Solutions",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Squaring Both Sides:</strong> When solving an inequality with moduli on both sides, such as \\(|ax+b| < |cx+d|\\), squaring both sides is fully valid because both quantities are non-negative: \\((ax+b)^2 < (cx+d)^2\\). This quickly reduces to a standard quadratic inequality.</p><p><strong>Single Modulus Pitfall:</strong> Do NOT square both sides if one side can be negative (e.g. \\(|2x-1| > x - 3\\)). Squaring can introduce extraneous solutions or flip inequality signs unpredictably. Instead, sketch the linear graphs or split into two linear cases: \\(2x-1 > x-3\\) and \\(2x-1 < -(x-3)\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Solve the inequality \\(|3x - 2| < |x + 6|\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>Since both sides are non-negative, square both sides:</p>\\[(3x - 2)^2 < (x + 6)^2\\]\\[9x^2 - 12x + 4 < x^2 + 12x + 36\\]\\[8x^2 - 24x - 32 < 0\\]\\[x^2 - 3x - 4 < 0\\]<p>Factor the quadratic:</p>\\[(x - 4)(x + 1) < 0\\]<p>The solution set is the interval between the roots:</p>\\[-1 < x < 4\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
